### Design Rationale Summary:

| Task | Rule Type | Why |
|------|-----------|-----|
| find birch_button | position_near_with_facing | "Find" task — player must navigate near and look at the target. Target at (3,1,-3) relative to spawn. |
| mine acacia_stairs | inventory_has | "Mine" task — mined item ends up in inventory. Player starts with 0 acacia_stairs. |
| mine black_wool | inventory_has (min_count=3) | "Mine" task — mined item ends up in inventory. Requires 3 because the crafting chain needs 3 wool. |
| craft to light_gray_bed | inventory_has | "Craft" task — crafted item ends up in inventory. Player starts with 0 light_gray_bed. |

### Key Notes:
- **No position_inside_box** used since no task is purely about navigation/movement.
- **mine black_wool requires min_count=3** because the player needs exactly 3 black_wool to dye into 3 light_gray_wool for the bed recipe. This ensures the milestone only triggers when the player has gathered sufficient materials.
- **mine acacia_stairs requires only min_count=1** since the stairs are a gate task (planks are pre-given in inventory); mining even 1 stair confirms task completion.
- All items checked are bare names without "minecraft:" prefix per the evaluator specification.

